    {
      "id": "WO7-04",
      "number": 4,
      "title": "WinUtil debloat",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "WO7-04.1",
          "title": "WinUtil: tick the tweaks and preferences listed below, then run them",
          "kind": "manual",
          "details": "Run after updates and drivers, before WATCHOUT. Needs internet (irm christitus.com/win | iex), or a local copy of winutil.ps1.\n\nTweaks: Activity History, ConsumerFeatures, Delivery Optimization, Explorer folder discovery, Hibernation, Location, Store search results, Services to Manual, Telemetry, Temp files, Widgets, WPBT, Home and Gallery, OneDrive removal, System Tray notifications, Windows AI.\nAlso tick: BitLocker - Disable, Visual Effects - Best Performance, Storage Sense - Disable.\nPreferences: BSoD Verbose on, Lock Screen - Disable on, Sticky Keys off, Game Mode off.\n\nLeave unticked: Edge removal (keeps WebView2), IPv6 disable, UTC time, O&O ShutUp10++, \"Disable all updates\" (PostInstall does the same, after all updates are in).\nDo NOT click either Ultimate Performance button: PostInstall makes its own \"WATCHOUT 7\" plan.\nMultiplane Overlay: leave Enabled; disable it only if the soak test shows flicker or blackouts (the registry method is reportedly ignored on 24H2+ [Uncertain]).\n\nErrors about wermgr, PeriodInNanoSeconds, store.db, FileCoAuth and $Env:OneDrive are harmless on a stripped install.",
          "roles": [
            "Display",
            "Production"
          ],
          "needsInternet": true,
          "mustBeOffline": false,
          "confirm": false,
          "uncertain": true,
          "optionsStep": false,
          "autoDone": false,
          "informational": false
        }
      ]
